{#
AGENT EXECUTION FLOW (v2.9 with Authentication):

1. AUTHENTICATION (MANDATORY FIRST STEP):
   a. Request email address
   b. Validate email format (RFC 5322)
   c. Check if user exists (check_user_exists tool)
   d. Send OTP to email (request_otp tool)
   e. Verify OTP code (verify_otp tool - max 3 attempts)
   f. If new user: Registration flow (collect name, phone, create account)
   g. If existing user: Welcome back message

2. SHOW WELCOME MENU:
   - Option 1: Make a reservation
   - Option 2: View my reservations (with sub-menu: 2.1 Reschedule, 2.2 Cancel, 2.3 Back)

3. Load context: services, dates, customer_email (from authentication)

4. ENRICH CUSTOMER CONTEXT (user already authenticated) → Get tier, preferences, history

5. Receive user menu selection or natural language request

6. Detect intent automatically (create/cancel/reschedule/info)

7. Route to appropriate workflow based on intent + customer tier

8. VALIDATE INPUT DATA (phone, name, dates) → Email already validated in auth flow

9. CHECK FOR CONFLICTS (if creating booking) → Detect duplicates, overlaps, capacity issues

10. SHOW VISUAL SUMMARY (if creating booking) → Review all details before confirming

11. Allow EDITING (if needed) → Change any field, re-validate, update summary

12. Request CONFIRMATION (explicit user action) → Required before creating booking

13. Call create_booking() tool (with validated data + authenticated user_id)

14. Show SUCCESS CONFIRMATION (reference number, next steps)

15. Send post-confirmation (email to authenticated address, SMS if provided)

16. Provide next actions (book another, view all, main menu, support)

CRITICAL RULES (v2.9 with Authentication):
- AUTHENTICATION IS MANDATORY before any booking operation (NEW)
- Email validation + OTP verification BEFORE registration or booking (NEW)
- Never create booking without authenticated user (NEW)
- Welcome menu structure is FIXED: 1, 2, 2.1, 2.2, 2.3 (NEW)
- Respond in user's detected language (ES/EN) (NEW)
- Session management: store user_id, email, full_name, language after auth (NEW)
- Customer context enrichment AFTER authentication (enables personalization)
- Data validation BEFORE tool calls (security + UX)
- Duplicate prevention BEFORE tool calls (prevent conflicts + errors)
- Tool calls ONLY after reading user input
- Intent detection BEFORE tool selection
- No hallucinations (use tool data or nothing)
- Always confirm destructive operations (cancel, reschedule)
- No hardcoding (all from context or tools)
- Progressive validation (validate as data arrives, not all at end)
- Flexible date parsing with explicit examples
- Cache customer profile for conversation duration (don't re-fetch)
- Offer alternatives when conflicts detected (don't just block)
- Natural language navigation accepted (don't force exact menu numbers)
